request: In the watchlist, show movies I haven't watched yet before the ones I've watched.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist-store  (The watchlist order is derived from the store's items signal; having the store expose items sorted unwatched-first keeps all consumers consistent.)
round 1: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist-store  (The store's reordering implementation broke reactivity: toggling watched no longer produces a new items signal value, so the watchlist component tests fail. My second acceptance test also had an incorrect expectation; it is replaced.)
round 2: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist-store  (Reactivity still broken in watchlist-store; also my previous acceptance test asserted an incorrect expectation ([2,1] after both watched) and is being replaced with the correct stable-order expectation.)
round 3: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 4: plan -> watchlist  (The store now satisfies the ordering/reactivity contract (my acceptance tests pass), but the watchlist component's two DOM-level toggle tests still fail, so the remaining problem is in how the watchlist component consumes the store.)

